From f3830d3f3b1c33a19988828d4ddf81bd7801d89a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 19:34:13 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] prplmesh: controller/bwl/monitor/nl80211 fixes for stability
 and correctness

controller/bwl/monitor: preserve STA DM stats and ClientCapabilities on restart
- After prplmesh stop/start while STAs are associated, re-query
  ClientCapabilities, preserve uplink RCPI / link metrics stats, and
  re-trigger connected-clients events so the DM is fully populated
  without waiting for the next association frame

bwl/nl80211: skip associated STAs in unassoc RSSI measurement
- add_peer_neighbor() rejects STAs currently associated on the radio
  with EEXIST; skip them so the ROC scan proceeds with only truly
  unassociated STAs and valid RCPI results are returned

nl80211: MLO STA_Connected assoc frame fallback
- STA_Connected uses the MLD MAC as src_mac but m_latest_assoc_frame
  is keyed by the link MAC; scan by BSSID match when direct lookup
  fails so the association frame is found and ClientCapabilities are
  correctly populated for MLO clients

Signed-off-by: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
